# The public origin of the deployed site.
#
# This drives every <link rel="canonical">, the sitemap, robots.txt and the
# og:image URLs. It must be the real, final origin — including https — or
# search engines and social cards will point at the wrong host.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://igitur.xyz

# ── Market data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Leave both unset and the site runs on deterministic figures generated from
# the ticker text, with a warning on every page that carries a number. Set them
# and those warnings disappear on their own, because they are derived from the
# data rather than written beside it.
#
# Vendor: Financial Modeling Prep. Chosen because it batches — the whole
# universe in a handful of requests, which is what makes a free tier workable
# for a site that renders 163 tickers on one page. Sign up at
# https://site.financialmodelingprep.com/developer/docs and the key appears in
# the dashboard.
#
# The code calls FMP's /stable API, not the older /api/v3: v3 is legacy and a
# key created today does not reach it. If /status reports that the vendor is
# not answering, it prints what the vendor actually said — 401 or 403 is a bad
# key, 402 is a plan without batch quotes, 429 is the daily quota.
# Leave BOTH unset and the site uses Yahoo's public chart endpoint: no key, no
# account, no signup, real prices. That is the default because an account signup
# was the only thing standing between this deployment and real data for weeks.
#
# It is not a supported API — it is what Yahoo's own charts call, public and
# unauthenticated, and Yahoo may restrict it without notice. It also does not
# carry market capitalisation, which then shows as an em dash rather than a
# made-up number. FMP is the sturdier supplier; set a key and it takes over.
#
# MARKET_PROVIDER=fmp | yahoo | synthetic   (default: fmp if a key is set, else yahoo)
MARKET_PROVIDER=
MARKET_API_KEY=

# How long a quote is reused, in seconds. Default 3600.
#
# This is set by the vendor's daily allowance, not by taste. One refresh of the
# universe costs 4 requests (163 tickers, batched 50 at a time) and the free
# tier is 250 a day, so a one-minute TTL spends the whole allowance inside an
# hour and the site quietly falls back to synthetic for the rest of the day.
# An hour costs 96 a day and leaves room for /track and the record.
#
# Lower it only on a paid plan.
# MARKET_TTL_S=3600

# ── Social handles ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Leave these unset and the site renders no social links at all, and no card
# attribution. That is deliberate: /token promises the contract address appears
# "here and on X at the same moment, and nowhere else first", and /legal
# promises "any page that does is not us". Pointing those at a handle nobody
# here owns hands the project's name to whoever registers it.
#
# Both accounts are held, so the real handles are defaults in lib/site.ts rather
# than settings — a build that forgot these must not silently un-launch the
# channels on a live site. Set them only to point a fork or a staging deploy
# somewhere else. Unlike the market key, these are read at BUILD time, so a
# change needs a rebuild, not just a restart.
#
# A value that is not handle-shaped (a single space will do) removes that link
# again, prose included.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_X_HANDLE=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TELEGRAM_HANDLE=
